 <a name="consent-used"></a>
-<h4>AuditEvent indicating authorizing Consent</h4>
+<h4>AuditEvent and Provenance indicating authorizing Consent</h4>
 <p>
 <em>Use case:</em> For any given Resource, there is a need to determine the Consent that authorized the 
-given Resource to be created or updated. For example, a Privacy audit tracking down some data was recorded 
+given Resource to be created, updated, or deleted. For example, a Privacy audit tracking down some data was recorded
 when it is reported that the data should not have been gathered.
 </p>
 <p>
-  <em>Trigger:</em> When there is a need to trace Resource create / update that were authorized by a Consent.
+  <em>Trigger:</em> When there is a need to trace Resource create, update, or delete activities that were authorized by a Consent.
 </p>
 <p>
-  <em>Approach:</em> AuditEvent can <a href="security.html#6.1.0.5.1">record Access Control decisions</a> including permit and deny, and can indicate when that Access Control decision included rules from a Patient's Consent (e.g., <a href="auditevent-example-consent-authz.html">Example Consent recorded in the AuditEvent as an AuditEvent.entity</a>).
+  <em>Approach:</em> AuditEvent can <a href="security.html#6.1.0.5.1">record Access Control decisions</a> including permit and deny, and can indicate when that Access Control decision included rules from a Patient's Consent (e.g., <a href="auditevent-example-consent-authz.html">Example Consent recorded in the AuditEvent as an AuditEvent.entity</a>). Provenance can memorialize that a create, update, or delete activity was authorized by Consent by identifying the affected resource as <code>Provenance.target</code> and the authorizing Consent or related AuditEvent as <code>Provenance.entity.what</code> (e.g., <a href="provenance-example5.html">authorizing AuditEvent</a>, <a href="provenance-example6.html">authorizing Consent</a>).
 </p>
 
